# Deliberately EMPTY of LFS rules — do not re-add `*.tflite filter=lfs`.
#
# The two moderation models (app/src/main/assets/moderation/{nsfw,toxicity}.tflite, ~32 MB total) are
# stored as ordinary Git blobs because F-Droid's buildserver has no Git LFS support (fdroidserver issue
# #1190, open since 2024). A checkout without a working LFS client yields 130-byte pointer stubs, and
# NsfwImageModerator / MlTextModerator both degrade *silently* to allow-all on an unreadable model — so
# LFS here means F-Droid would ship a quietly unmoderated app that also fails reproducible-build
# verification. Plain blobs make that impossible; the build additionally hard-fails on a stub model
# (see the checkModerationModels task in app/build.gradle.kts).

# `.agents/memory/decisions.md` is a generated router (`python3 scripts/adr.py index`)
# over `.agents/memory/decisions/`, and its only churn is appended table rows — one per
# new ADR. This repo is worked in several git worktrees at once; each one adding a
# decision conflicts on that append every time, and the resolution is always "keep both
# rows". `merge=union` does exactly that automatically, which is the whole point of the
# one-file-per-decision split (see the script's header).
#
# Union can duplicate a line if two branches edit the *preamble* rather than the table.
# That is not a merge to resolve by hand either: rerun `python3 scripts/adr.py index`
# and it overwrites the file wholesale. `python3 scripts/adr.py index --check` proves
# the committed router matches the files it describes, and CI runs it.
.agents/memory/decisions.md merge=union
